   $q$Listen. Washing your hands helps get rid of tiny germs that can make you sick. First, wet your hands with clean water from the sink. Next, rub your hands with soap for about twenty seconds, which is about as long as singing a short song two times. Then rinse off all the soap under the water. Last, dry your hands with a clean towel. What do you use right after you wet your hands? Tap the answer.$q$, $q$[{"text":"soap","is_correct":true,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"soap"}},{"text":"a towel","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"a towel"}},{"text":"a crayon","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"a crayon"}}]$q$::jsonb, $q$soap$q$, $q$First you wet your hands. Next you rub them with soap. The towel comes last, after you rinse.$q$, 'draft', null, 'audio_picture', null)
