  ('c1b474b6-c269-5155-a64f-34d5ecfc5020', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g2-connections'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Listen. Long ago, no one had ever flown an airplane. Two brothers, Orville and Wilbur Wright, spent years building and testing gliders, which fly with no engine. Then they added an engine and propellers to their flying machine. In nineteen oh three, Orville flew it for twelve seconds over the sand near Kitty Hawk, North Carolina. That short flight helped lead to the planes people ride today. What did the brothers add to their flying machine? Tap the answer.$q$, $q$[{"text":"a sail","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"a sail"}},{"text":"an engine","is_correct":true,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"an engine"}},{"text":"a balloon","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"a balloon"}}]$q$::jsonb, $q$an engine$q$, $q$First the brothers tested gliders with no engine. Then they added an engine and propellers, and their machine flew.$q$, 'draft', null, 'audio_picture', null)
