   $q$Listen. In spring, a robin builds a nest in a tree. First, it gathers twigs, grass and mud. Then it sits in the middle and presses with its body to shape the nest into a round cup that will hold eggs. The mother robin lays blue eggs in the cup and keeps them warm. About two weeks later, the chicks hatch, hungry for worms. Why does the robin press with its body? Tap the answer.$q$, $q$[{"text":"to make a cup shape","is_correct":true,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"to make a cup shape"}},{"text":"to break the eggs","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"to break the eggs"}},{"text":"to find worms","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"to find worms"}}]$q$::jsonb, $q$to make a cup shape$q$, $q$The robin presses with its body to shape the nest into a round cup. The cup holds the eggs safely.$q$, 'draft', null, 'audio_picture', null)
