   $q$Listen. Long ago, people traveled far by walking, riding horses, or riding in wagons pulled by horses. A long trip across the country could take months. Then steam trains were built, and they could go much faster than wagons. Later, cars and airplanes came along. Today, a trip that once took months can take just a few hours by plane. Which way to travel came after wagons and went much faster? Tap the picture.$q$, $q$[{"text":"train","is_correct":true,"tile":{"kind":"object_group","image":"train","count":1}},{"text":"wagon","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"object_group","image":"wagon","count":1}},{"text":"horse","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"object_group","image":"horse","count":1}}]$q$::jsonb, $q$train$q$, $q$First people walked, rode horses or rode in wagons. Then trains came, and they went much faster than wagons.$q$, 'draft', null, 'audio_picture', null)
