   $q$Listen. Snow begins high up in the clouds. When it is very cold up there, tiny drops of water freeze into bits of ice. The ice grows into lacy snowflakes, often with six points. When the snowflakes get heavy enough, they fall toward the ground. But if the air near the ground is warm, they melt on the way down and fall as rain. What falls if the air near the ground is warm? Tap the picture.$q$, $q$[{"text":"rain","is_correct":true,"tile":{"kind":"object_group","image":"rain","count":1}},{"text":"snow","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"object_group","image":"snow","count":1}},{"text":"leaf","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"object_group","image":"leaf","count":1}}]$q$::jsonb, $q$rain$q$, $q$Snowflakes fall from cold clouds. If the air near the ground is warm, they melt on the way down, so rain falls instead of snow.$q$, 'draft', null, 'audio_picture', null)
